# Copy to .env and fill in. Every VITE_ variable the code reads is compiled
# into the app bundle, so nothing here may be secret.

# IGDB credentials (Twitch client ID / secret) live ONLY in Supabase secrets
# (TWITCH_CLIENT_ID / TWITCH_CLIENT_SECRET), used by the igdb-proxy Edge Function.
# Never add them here.

# IGDB proxy: the deployed igdb-proxy Supabase Edge Function URL.
# All IGDB traffic goes through it; without it, game data does not load.
VITE_IGDB_PROXY_URL=

# Public web origin for links that leave the app (password-reset redirect).
# Must be allow-listed in Supabase -> Authentication -> URL Configuration.
# VITE_PUBLIC_APP_URL=

# Supabase: Project Settings -> API (the anon key is public by design).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Outward-facing links (read only by src/config/site.js) -----------------
# Each is optional. A feature whose value is missing is hidden, never faked:
#   no VITE_SITE_URL      -> share actions send text without a link, and the
#                            Privacy Policy / Terms rows are hidden
#   no VITE_SUPPORT_EMAIL -> "Send feedback" is hidden
#   no VITE_APP_STORE_ID  -> "Rate the app" is hidden
#   no VITE_BUILD_NUMBER  -> the "(build N)" suffix is hidden

# Origin of the static site deployed from /web (see web/README.md),
# e.g. https://yourdomain.com — no trailing slash, no path.
# VITE_SITE_URL=

# Address behind Settings -> Help & about -> Send feedback.
# VITE_SUPPORT_EMAIL=

# Numeric App Store ID, available once the app exists in App Store Connect.
# VITE_APP_STORE_ID=

# CFBundleVersion of the build being shipped.
# VITE_BUILD_NUMBER=

# --- Checkpoint Plus (read only by src/services/plusService.js) -------------
# RevenueCat -> Project -> API keys -> the iOS app's PUBLIC SDK key (appl_...).
# Public by design. Without it everything Plus is hidden (badge, Settings
# rows, purchases). The RevenueCat SECRET key and the webhook secret live only
# in Supabase secrets (REVENUECAT_API_KEY, REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_SECRET).
# VITE_REVENUECAT_IOS_KEY=

# --- Ads for free users (read only by src/services/adsService.js) ------------
# AdMob -> Apps -> your iOS app. Both are public identifiers (they ship inside
# every app that shows ads), not secrets. Without BOTH, no ads are requested
# and no ad space is reserved.
#   VITE_ADMOB_APP_ID       ca-app-pub-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX~YYYYYYYYYY
#   VITE_ADMOB_BANNER_IOS   ca-app-pub-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX/ZZZZZZZZZZ (Banner unit)
# Ads are non-personalized and never trigger the App Tracking Transparency
# prompt. Development builds (`npm run dev`, `npm run build:dev`) always show
# Google's sample test ads instead of the real unit.
#
# ALSO required, once, in Xcode (Info.plist reads GADApplicationIdentifier from
# a build setting, because Xcode does not read this file): App target ->
# Build Settings -> + -> Add User-Defined Setting -> ADMOB_APP_ID, and give it
# the same value as VITE_ADMOB_APP_ID. If the .env value is set but this
# setting is empty, the app crashes when the first banner is requested.
# VITE_ADMOB_APP_ID=
# VITE_ADMOB_BANNER_IOS=
